WEBVTT

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.040
It's a real mess, just like the rumors said.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.930
What is this place?

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.820
A graveyard of ships.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.140
There was a battle here
during ancient times.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.920
Our dear ancestors sure blew each other to hell and back.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.180
These things barely resemble ships anymore.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.580
Everyone knows the story.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.110
Don't be like that.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.420
Our job is to search every ship we find that looks remotely salvageable.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.070
Ridget's orders, remember?

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.340
This is still a bust, however you look at it.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.540
The few ships that survived intact have already rusted away.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:03.740
So what do we do?

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.410
Nothing really looks worth searching.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.280
Let's withdraw in a bit.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:10.880
Bellows.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:11.710
Yeah?

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.630
I'm below you.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:14.670
How about this ship?

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.960
It doesn't look too heavily damaged.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:18.640
Let's see.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.780
Good catch, Ledo!

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:38.740
I'd like to take a closer look.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.750
May I go inside?

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.580
I'll go too.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.630
Looks like a cargo vessel.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:02.930
It's been down here for some time,

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.060
but it's surprisingly well-preserved.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.850
Isn't that...

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.820
A core unit!

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.280
We can make a new Yunboro with this!

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:18.590
Great job, Ledo!

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:20.240
Hey! How's the outside?

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:24.700
I'm at the stern. No apparent damage.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.700
She might've been scuttled.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.670
Same with the bow. It's a joy to look at.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.870
Great! Hey, Ledo...

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:33.610
Huh?

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.300
Of course it doesn't work now.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.140
That's what you really care about, huh?

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:49.950
Researching the ancient civilization.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:51.590
"Archeology," was it?

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:52.110
Yeah.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:56.250
If I can restore some of the data,
I might find out more

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.110
about the world people lived in
when this ship was built.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:04.870
I'll be sure to bring all that stuff
to the surface too.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.230
Thanks.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.270
Bellows!

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.170
What's wrong?

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.240
Look at this! Over here!

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.100
There's a huge trench!

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.560
Here too!

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.600
We can pass under the bilge!

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.310
That means we can pull cables
under it with the Yunboros.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.920
Looks like we found one heck of a haul!

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:41.280
The Ocean Routes Stretch into the Distance

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:41.280
[ Part 1 ]

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.570
deai to wakare wo

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.570
On our long journey,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:59.860
mune ni dakitomete susumou

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:59.860
let us remember the people we met and parted from

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:06.970
kioku wa itsumo yawaraka na tezawari de

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:06.970
Their memory always casts a gentle smile

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:11.180
hohoemikakete kureru

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:11.180
on the present day

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:18.610
sora no nioi to nami ga zawameku uta

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:18.610
I can smell the sky and hear the waves sing

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:24.740
nanigenai shiawase ga afuredashite

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:24.740
From this simple happiness

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:29.680
hajimari no yuuki mitsuketa

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:29.680
I derived my courage

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:33.670
mawaru yo mawaru yo

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:33.670
The world goes on

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:37.070
sekai wa mawaru yo

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:37.070
The world goes ever on

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.950
kokoro no hane hiroge

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.950
We spread the wings of our souls

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:44.760
bokura wa kyou wo ikiteyuku

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:44.760
and live our lives

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.960
tatoe donna kaze ga fuitemo

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.960
no matter what the times may bring

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:54.200
nandodemo jiyuu wo motomete

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:54.200
We will seek freedom

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:59.140
habataite yukou

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:59.140
like the birds

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:03.390
kanashimi wo norikoeta saki ni

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:03.390
We will find happiness

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:08.330
hikari ga aru kara

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:08.330
past whatever hardship there may be

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:58.840
Leema!

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:02.460
This way!

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.550
Coming!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.640
This is the distribution center.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.980
Are they all messengers?

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:19.810
That's right.

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:25.200
We collect items that people post across the fleet, and we hand them in here.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.150
And then...

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:30.230
we get delivery jobs in return.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.690
I see.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.030
Amy!

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.320
Hey there!

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:35.910
Melty! Saya!

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.620
Perfect timing!

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.420
How's the work?

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.570
Gotten the hang of it?

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.860
I'm learning bit by bit.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.760
With Amy as your mentor,
you'll pick it up in a flash!

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.380
Right! I'll do my best!

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:52.720
Listen up, girls!

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:54.810
We've got afternoon deliveries!

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:56.570
Gotcha!

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.390
Good thing we can
split it three ways, huh?

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.240
It's been a while since
we all got the same area.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:08.190
So then he asked me, "What present
would a girl like you be happy with?"

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.330
I'd love some new shoes.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:11.660
Mine are always wearing out.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:14.870
That's not the point!
Does he have to ask <i>me</i>?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.580
It's a bit inconsiderate, I guess.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:18.790
Right?

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.330
Can't you just ignore him?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.080
Easy for you to say with
a boyfriend waiting for you!

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.210
Jeez.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.050
I'll take that.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:27.800
All done!

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:32.440
See, if we split it up like this,
it makes things much easier.

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:35.220
Well, let's get going!

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:45.980
Bye!

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.360
See you later!

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.460
I'm not too familiar with
the ships in this area yet.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:53.680
Over there!

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:59.790
These ships are from the fleet I
joined with, so I know them well.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:01.330
And over there...

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.540
is where I live.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.360
Okay! Looks good to me!

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.280
Hey! Come over here!

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.180
Roger!

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.370
Hey! That's dangerous!

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.790
This is no place for amateurs!

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.320
Sorry!

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.860
Sorry, Mayta!

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:53.080
Leema, you shouldn't bother them
when they're working.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:54.910
Sorry.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:55.510
Um...

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.500
Are you an engineer?

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.320
Huh? Yeah.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:02.470
So how do you manufacture this part?

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.020
What's the composition of the alloy?
What torque of actuator do you use?

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:13.240
If you're that keen on machines,
you should come and work with us!

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.950
We could use all the help we can get!

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.700
Hold it right there, Pinion!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.080
Thanks, Mr. Pompadour!

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:22.070
Pompadour...

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:27.120
But for now, I'd like to
learn more about Gargantia!

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.580
Welcome back, Ledo.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:43.260
Thanks.

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.600
Good job finding this one.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:52.860
Let's see if we can pull it up again in one piece.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:57.860
We've been short on ships
ever since taking in Kugel's fleet.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.040
It's not exactly small.

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:00.950
Where would we put it?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.650
We can harvest the Chrono's farms early.

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:06.840
That should do it.

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:09.120
Sounds like a plan.

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:12.340
This'll be fun!

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:22.760
Ledo!

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:24.470
Thanks for waiting!

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:26.180
Amy!

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:29.140
Let's go! I'm drenched in sweat!

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:53.880
Man, a bath after work is a gift from the heavens!

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:59.690
Hey, Ledo. I heard they decided to
pull up the sunken ship you found.

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:00.680
Yeah.

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:06.110
It's been a while since I last
got to use my secret weapon.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:06.970
Secret weapon?

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:10.690
That's right! It's quite a show,
so look forward to it!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.860
Leema showed me around the Kugel fleet.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:22.070
You're pretty organized for your age.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:23.690
It's no big deal.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:24.910
"For your age," huh?

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:27.870
She's only a year younger than you, Melty.

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:32.420
Everyone's here, I see!

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:34.790
Hello!

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:38.510
Amy, Ledo was the real MVP today.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:40.160
Really?

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:43.090
He didn't say anything about it to me, though.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:47.060
Oh, you came together again?
Glad to see you're getting along.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.650
Gargantia sure has an impressive
assortment of facilities.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:00.940
Hello! A marine mix for me!

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:01.860
Me too!

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:04.030
And for me...

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:05.480
Look, it's the ex-pirate queen.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:09.230
Learn some respect!

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:12.040
That's "pirate queen on vacation" to you.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:14.350
She calls herself that?

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:17.500
My break's almost over, though.

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:20.870
You're doing a big salvage op soon, right?

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:25.130
We've been tasked with securing
the area so no one gets in the way.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:29.430
In other words, we've been hired as bodyguards.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.390
Whoa.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:32.250
So you <i>do</i> work.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.580
Quiet, you.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.080
You're Ledo?

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:45.910
And you?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:50.040
I'm Leema. Amy's showing me the ropes at work.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:51.820
You're a messenger?

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.500
I wanna hear your stories!

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:58.460
Please tell me about the
flying Yunboro you rode in!

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:01.670
Chamber?

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:08.780
He was...

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.770
a machine built to fight.

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.590
He used gravity manipulation to fly.

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.390
He could understand any language,

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:22.740
and he used the immense power
at his disposal to protect his pilot.

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.610
The ultimate battle armor,

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:26.900
a Machine Caliber.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:29.270
No...

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:35.040
He was Chamber.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:41.080
So he really was the same as
the sky god's divine messenger.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.560
Sky god?

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:47.720
Do you mean Colonel Kugel's Striker?

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:52.680
Yeah. I'm from Lord Kugel's fleet.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.570
You are?

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:59.410
Could you tell me what happened to the Colonel and Striker?

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:03.370
Cutie spotted!

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.190
What's this? Do I see someone flirting?

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:07.140
Two-timing, even?

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:09.490
Can't say I blame you, Leema.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.480
It's not like that!

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:18.590
Ledo, girls need constant attention,
or they start to worry!

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:20.790
Yep! And that goes for Amy too!

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:26.970
Remember how she'd ask Chamber for advice in secret?

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:36.730
So, uh, is there something Ledo would,
you know, like to have?

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:38.900
Chamber?

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:44.520
The food and other supplies necessary
for the Lieutenant's daily operation

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:46.650
are already provided to him on a steady basis.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.900
That's not what I meant!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:53.460
I mean, like, something that'll
make him happy or something.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:57.120
You know, something that'll put a smile on his face!

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.380
It has already been ascertained that the Alliance's recreation program

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.920
is ineffective on the Lieutenant.

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.260
That's not what I mean.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:14.660
How can I get to know Ledo better?

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:18.480
H-How do you know about that?!

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.880
Uh, well...

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.850
It's just advice, right?

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:25.080
Never mind that stuff!

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.140
Amy?

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:28.150
What's this?

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:29.690
A lovers' spat?

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:31.130
Must be nice to be young.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.240
I'm almost jealous.

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.370
Oh, come on!

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:38.480
Ledo, I'm glad to see you're
doing so well for yourself,

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:40.590
but work's important too!

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:45.170
Salvaging's one thing, but have you
gotten a taste for engineering yet?

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.460
What are you talking about, Pinion?

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:51.300
He's been teaching me a bit
about how Yunboros work.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:53.940
Are you kidding me?

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:58.010
I just felt sorry for him, taking orders from such a hardass all the time.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:00.270
Who're you calling a hardass?

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:01.230
You.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.230
Leema.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:02.230
Y-Yes?

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:11.650
I've always wondered how the
Colonel's fleet turned out the way it did.

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.010
Could you tell me?

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:30.510
My home ship joined the fleet back when Lord Kugel and his messenger began guiding the people.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:37.710
The fleet was united by the worship
of the sky god's emissary, Lord Kugel.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:41.090
But after the whalesquids were defeated

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:46.170
and Priestesses Linaria and Aleria
passed away, everything changed.

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:52.080
We gave everything we had to sustain the fleet.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:55.950
Even dying was just seen
as another way to contribute.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:00.400
"To stay strong, dispose of the weak."

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:02.780
"Convince those who can't fight

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:06.290
that sacrificing themselves for the good of the group is the greatest joy."

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:09.850
That is the way of the
Galactic Alliance of Humankind.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:13.920
I find it hard to believe that the
Colonel would have wanted that, though.

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:16.520
I don't know.

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:22.930
No one even knows exactly
when Lord Kugel lost his life.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:30.010
If he'd still been alive,
I'm certain we would have found a way.

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:36.550
I owed my life to him many times over.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:48.460
I haven't been able to find anything of the sort.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:52.140
It's not easy to find out more about Chamber.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:52.920
Yeah.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:58.780
I hoped we could find out more from the ejected cockpit that remained,

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:04.890
but the technology used is far beyond
even that of the ancients.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:10.760
These are all the scriptures my sister Linaria inherited from our father.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:13.120
We're sorry that we couldn't be of help.

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:18.110
That's not true at all. There is so much in these books that we of Gargantia did not know.

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:22.760
Humanity realized that their
planet's days were numbered,

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:26.090
and most joined one of two rivaling factions.

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:32.170
But some, few in number as they were,
decided to look for another path.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:35.090
We are the descendants of those people.

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:39.920
All of humanity tried to survive in any way they could.

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:45.680
Those who left for the stars amidst that conflict must have felt the same way.

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:49.770
They abandoned Earth?

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:56.170
Even so, I'd like to believe it was a
difficult decision for them to make.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:29.400
I know what happened to the people who left Earth.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:32.090
I'm the only one here who does.

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:35.080
There has to be something I can do.

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:36.480
I'm sure of it.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:42.140
I've been trying to find a way to
communicate with the whalesquids.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:46.120
There might be a better way for
us to live, without conflict.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:50.600
Maybe I'm just trying to make amends.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.460
I don't get it.

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:56.120
Why do you feel responsible?

00:19:56.120 --> 00:20:00.170
Amy, I live in fear every day.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:00.840
Huh?

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:07.340
The Alliance is still fighting an
all-out war with the Hideauze.

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:11.950
And deep inside, I actually feel like it's a necessary war.

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:15.900
But... You're here with us now!

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:19.110
The galactic war you came from
is far, far away, right?

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.680
So it's not relevant anymore!

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.200
You don't have to worry!

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:27.400
No, it's very relevant. Everything...

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:30.830
Everything humanity does,
be it here or there, is connected.

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:41.180
If we ever came into conflict with the whalesquids,

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:43.690
or if the Hideauze found Earth,

00:20:43.690 --> 00:20:47.220
would I be able to handle it
differently from the Alliance?

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.600
Could I find another way?

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:55.540
What if I couldn't?

00:20:55.540 --> 00:21:00.010
What if I too had to throw away
something precious just to stay alive?

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:05.950
Ledo...

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:09.670
It wouldn't come down to that.

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:14.410
You'd find a way. Just like back then.

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:20.620
You and Chamber did so much
to help us during that huge storm.

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:25.790
The huge storm...

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:32.400
Leema, you were listening?

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:34.840
I didn't intend to—

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:38.270
I mean, yes I did.

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:45.530
Please tell me what happened with
Ledo and Chamber in that storm!

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:05.800
One of the boats got torn loose
and dashed against the hull!

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:07.380
Check for leaks!

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.040
The bulkheads are closed!

00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:11.510
Okay! But check anyway!

00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:32.660
That's the last one!

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:33.490
Over to you!

00:22:33.970 --> 00:22:35.700
Roger! Moving along!

00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:44.800
Secured!

00:22:45.110 --> 00:22:46.880
Okay! Pull the crane!

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:55.770
Connection complete!

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:58.600
All right! Keep it up!

00:22:58.600 --> 00:22:59.980
Good job, Ledo!

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:14.030
What is it?

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:16.080
It's an emergency!

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:19.520
The Artemia's interlocks are damaged!

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:20.460
What?!

00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:23.560
Tell me the details.

00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:26.380
The support wires have all snapped,

00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:28.540
and the interlock pylons are damaged.

00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:29.670
Only one is left.

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:31.400
What?

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:34.430
The screw pods on both
gunwales are inoperable?!

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:42.730
Commodore, more than five hundred
people live aboard the Artemia.

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:43.810
They are in danger!

00:23:44.850 --> 00:23:46.250
Any bridges?

00:23:46.250 --> 00:23:50.050
There's one left, but it could break any minute.

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:51.280
Can we repair the interlocks?

00:23:52.140 --> 00:23:53.750
We don't have the manpower.

00:23:53.750 --> 00:23:56.370
Immediate repairs are out of question.

00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:04.330
Urgent delivery!

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:06.150
It's a damage report!

00:24:09.780 --> 00:24:16.960
Allowing such a large ship to drift freely
would put the entire fleet at risk.

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:22.980
We will scuttle the Artemia.

00:24:26.340 --> 00:24:28.150
The Artemia?

00:24:29.870 --> 00:24:30.940
Understood.

00:24:31.790 --> 00:24:34.990
All personnel on the Artemia are to
evacuate immediately! Top priority!

00:24:35.450 --> 00:24:36.690
Scuttle the Artemia!

00:24:36.690 --> 00:24:37.780
Evacuate it right away!

00:24:39.150 --> 00:24:40.920
That's Saya's ship!

00:24:52.320 --> 00:24:53.280
This way!

00:24:53.280 --> 00:24:53.930
Hurry up!

00:24:58.500 --> 00:24:59.800
Amy!

00:24:59.800 --> 00:25:01.330
Where's Saya?

00:25:01.330 --> 00:25:02.510
She isn't here!

00:25:02.510 --> 00:25:04.100
She's still on board!

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:12.690
Not a chance! No!

00:25:13.080 --> 00:25:16.080
If she's to sink, I'm going down with her!

00:25:16.080 --> 00:25:18.570
Captain, stop being a child.

00:25:18.160 --> 00:25:21.080
I won't leave the ship I've lived my life on!

00:25:19.850 --> 00:25:21.080
Take him with you.

00:25:22.100 --> 00:25:24.260
We're going, Captain.

00:25:24.260 --> 00:25:26.040
No!

00:25:26.800 --> 00:25:29.690
My sister will oversee the evacuation.

00:25:29.690 --> 00:25:31.000
You guys leave too.

00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:32.460
Fleiss!

00:25:33.020 --> 00:25:35.120
We can't steer her anymore.

00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:37.800
There's no point staying on the bridge.

00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:39.470
Come on, get going!

00:25:44.820 --> 00:25:46.810
Bridge here!

00:25:46.810 --> 00:25:47.440
Brother!

00:25:48.210 --> 00:25:50.220
The central tower's empty!

00:25:50.220 --> 00:25:52.450
Okay! I'm the only one on the bridge too.

00:25:52.450 --> 00:25:53.350
Hurry with the rest!

00:25:53.350 --> 00:25:53.800
Okay!

00:25:53.800 --> 00:25:54.820
Saya!

00:25:55.360 --> 00:25:56.170
Amy!

00:25:56.170 --> 00:25:57.430
Why are you here?

00:25:57.430 --> 00:25:59.930
I heard the ship's being scuttled, so I was worried.

00:25:59.930 --> 00:26:02.240
I'm just making sure no one's been left behind.

00:26:02.240 --> 00:26:04.100
I'll help. What areas are left?

00:26:04.100 --> 00:26:06.010
The forecastle and the sterncastle.

00:26:06.010 --> 00:26:07.890
I'll check the forecastle, then.

00:26:07.890 --> 00:26:08.620
Thanks!

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:20.640
Is it true that we're abandoning the Artemia?

00:26:21.100 --> 00:26:21.720
Yeah!

00:26:22.060 --> 00:26:23.100
They're evacuating now!

00:26:23.770 --> 00:26:25.310
Are they gonna be all right?

00:26:29.200 --> 00:26:30.730
Is anyone still here?

00:26:31.110 --> 00:26:32.690
Evacuate now!

00:26:34.240 --> 00:26:35.310
Grandpa!

00:26:35.310 --> 00:26:36.360
You go ahead!

00:26:37.270 --> 00:26:38.030
Quickly!

00:26:38.730 --> 00:26:39.830
This way!

00:26:39.830 --> 00:26:41.030
Thank you.

00:26:43.220 --> 00:26:44.740
Thanks, lady!

00:26:50.060 --> 00:26:51.170
We're done!

00:26:51.170 --> 00:26:52.250
Just us now.

00:26:52.710 --> 00:26:54.250
Good job.

00:26:54.250 --> 00:26:56.460
Let's scuttle her and get out of here.

00:26:56.900 --> 00:26:58.950
Is this really the only way?

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:00.940
Destroying the ship?

00:27:00.940 --> 00:27:02.880
She can't be steered anymore.

00:27:02.880 --> 00:27:06.180
And with only one interlock left,
she could smash into the fleet.

00:27:07.110 --> 00:27:10.080
Better to sink her before it comes to that.

00:27:11.080 --> 00:27:13.400
I was born and raised here.

00:27:13.690 --> 00:27:16.610
I've never even heard of a storm this big.

00:27:18.430 --> 00:27:22.340
There are some things in life
that are simply beyond our control.

00:27:26.260 --> 00:27:27.340
This is the Artemia!

00:27:27.340 --> 00:27:30.750
There's a huge wave coming! Get out of there right now!

00:27:31.070 --> 00:27:33.230
Melty? I can't hear you properly!

00:27:33.230 --> 00:27:33.970
Say it again!

00:27:33.970 --> 00:27:34.660
Hurry!

00:27:34.660 --> 00:27:35.710
That!

00:28:15.870 --> 00:28:16.610
Everyone okay?

00:28:16.610 --> 00:28:17.360
Yeah!

00:28:17.360 --> 00:28:18.520
Look at that!

00:28:18.520 --> 00:28:19.260
What?

00:28:19.720 --> 00:28:20.550
No way.

00:28:29.110 --> 00:28:32.480
Detecting an abnormal angle
of inclination among the ships.

00:28:33.460 --> 00:28:34.020
Chamber!

00:28:36.280 --> 00:28:37.610
Amy! Saya!

00:28:37.610 --> 00:28:38.300
You okay?

00:28:38.300 --> 00:28:39.190
I'm fine!

00:29:00.420 --> 00:29:00.960
Ledo!

00:29:02.010 --> 00:29:04.430
We're close to capsizing!

00:29:09.260 --> 00:29:11.310
Chamber! Maximum output!

00:29:11.680 --> 00:29:12.550
Understood.

00:29:19.660 --> 00:29:21.650
Good, kiddo!

00:29:22.070 --> 00:29:23.410
Hold her!

00:29:23.410 --> 00:29:24.150
We can do this!

00:29:24.770 --> 00:29:26.240
Okay, reel it in!

00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:27.550
Roger!

00:29:36.680 --> 00:29:38.750
That's good! Keep it up!

00:29:40.150 --> 00:29:42.340
Look over there! We've got trouble!

00:29:46.530 --> 00:29:47.640
No way...

00:29:48.540 --> 00:29:50.100
What do we do now, Amy?

00:29:58.380 --> 00:30:00.480
Emergency broadcast intercepted.

00:30:01.220 --> 00:30:02.070
Listen!

00:30:02.750 --> 00:30:04.960
The Artemia's broken loose!

00:30:05.890 --> 00:30:08.480
Saya and Amy are still on board!

00:30:08.480 --> 00:30:09.360
What?!

00:30:11.510 --> 00:30:14.640
The vessel in question has lost
propulsion and steering ability.

00:30:14.640 --> 00:30:16.870
It is most likely out of control.

00:30:17.330 --> 00:30:18.930
It's adrift?

00:30:18.930 --> 00:30:19.860
Affirmative.

00:30:19.860 --> 00:30:20.380
Damn.

00:30:21.200 --> 00:30:23.190
I can't move from here!

00:30:23.190 --> 00:30:25.380
Straighten up, please!

00:30:31.010 --> 00:30:32.010
Just a little more!

00:30:32.010 --> 00:30:34.220
Ledo, metalhead...

00:30:43.270 --> 00:30:45.480
Get back inside and put these on!

00:30:45.480 --> 00:30:46.610
Okay!

00:30:49.450 --> 00:30:53.030
Crap, we're drifting back!

00:31:02.740 --> 00:31:04.670
Hull recovering.

00:31:05.680 --> 00:31:08.510
She's back! She stopped listing!

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:11.700
Declination returning to normal.

00:31:11.700 --> 00:31:13.970
Balance is likely to be restored.

00:31:14.340 --> 00:31:15.430
Okay!

00:32:00.880 --> 00:32:01.730
Ledo!

00:32:02.420 --> 00:32:04.860
Threat level lowering.

00:32:15.750 --> 00:32:17.280
That's amazing.

00:32:18.260 --> 00:32:21.720
I only managed thanks to Chamber.

00:32:21.720 --> 00:32:24.460
But he's gone now.

00:32:24.460 --> 00:32:27.740
I'm sure even if something like that happened now,

00:32:27.740 --> 00:32:30.010
you wouldn't give up.

00:32:31.660 --> 00:32:35.220
You've always done everything you could.

00:32:36.610 --> 00:32:38.430
That's the way you are.

00:33:17.400 --> 00:33:19.760
All right! Time to go down!

00:33:30.550 --> 00:33:33.650
Bellows! The capture vehicle is lowering at a steady pace!

00:33:33.650 --> 00:33:34.710
Got it!

00:33:34.710 --> 00:33:35.650
You all hear that?

00:33:36.030 --> 00:33:39.860
We're gonna raise a ship from her grave!

00:33:39.860 --> 00:33:41.960
This is a treasure among treasures!

00:33:41.960 --> 00:33:43.910
Lift her well!

00:33:43.910 --> 00:33:45.180
Roger!

00:33:52.870 --> 00:33:54.920
Recheck the area!

00:34:04.900 --> 00:34:07.070
Pinion! Letter for you!

00:34:07.070 --> 00:34:07.970
Thanks.

00:34:13.880 --> 00:34:16.740
Huh? You don't have any more deliveries?

00:34:18.650 --> 00:34:21.450
I saved this one for last.

00:34:22.280 --> 00:34:23.540
Oh? You're worried about Ledo?

00:34:24.540 --> 00:34:26.750
U-Uhh...

00:34:36.210 --> 00:34:39.080
Okay! Keep it up!

00:34:39.080 --> 00:34:40.890
Pinion! The anchors!

00:34:41.190 --> 00:34:42.290
Roger!

00:34:48.310 --> 00:34:50.650
Are you ready, guys?

00:34:51.450 --> 00:34:52.980
Let's get this done!

00:34:53.640 --> 00:34:56.970
Team one! Attach the guide wires to the hull!

00:35:07.170 --> 00:35:10.540
Team two! Pull the main wires under the hull!

00:35:10.950 --> 00:35:12.910
Confirm connection!

00:35:12.910 --> 00:35:14.590
Confirmed!

00:35:15.580 --> 00:35:17.590
Time to finish the job. Let's go.

00:35:18.410 --> 00:35:19.090
Roger.

00:35:32.350 --> 00:35:33.320
What's wrong?

00:35:33.320 --> 00:35:35.960
My wire got stuck on something!

00:35:44.790 --> 00:35:45.450
What?

00:35:47.870 --> 00:35:49.040
It's collapsing!

00:35:49.040 --> 00:35:50.500
Get out of there! Hurry!

00:36:02.920 --> 00:36:04.800
Go ahead! I've got this!

00:36:05.300 --> 00:36:06.510
Thanks!

00:36:26.900 --> 00:36:27.490
Are you okay?

00:36:27.840 --> 00:36:28.960
Ledo went under!

00:36:28.960 --> 00:36:29.940
What?

00:36:31.800 --> 00:36:32.960
Disconnect your cable!

00:36:37.490 --> 00:36:38.970
Ledo!

00:36:41.810 --> 00:36:43.240
No...

00:37:23.460 --> 00:37:24.880
How much air is left?

00:37:26.750 --> 00:37:28.100
This isn't good.

00:37:28.440 --> 00:37:30.010
Open reserve tank.

00:37:30.010 --> 00:37:32.310
Emergency injection of CO2 absorbent.

00:37:33.700 --> 00:37:35.270
Confirm battery power.

00:37:36.330 --> 00:37:36.980
Manipulator.

00:37:40.470 --> 00:37:41.750
Comms.

00:37:43.600 --> 00:37:44.710
This is Ledo!

00:37:47.220 --> 00:37:49.030
Don't tell me the communications cable...

00:37:51.690 --> 00:37:55.280
Someone respond! Please!

00:37:55.280 --> 00:37:56.500
This is Ledo!

00:38:12.600 --> 00:38:14.600
What happened down there?!

00:38:15.010 --> 00:38:16.430
I don't know.

00:38:16.430 --> 00:38:18.300
There was a sudden burst of gas,

00:38:18.300 --> 00:38:19.920
and the whole place collapsed.

00:38:19.920 --> 00:38:20.810
Where's Ledo?!

00:38:22.380 --> 00:38:26.150
Even if he's alive, his air won't last long.

00:38:27.160 --> 00:38:29.220
Then hurry up and dig him out!

00:38:29.220 --> 00:38:31.820
It's far too dangerous to go down there!

00:38:31.820 --> 00:38:33.710
The rescue party would get buried too.

00:38:35.190 --> 00:38:35.870
No...

00:38:37.680 --> 00:38:39.360
No way!

00:38:39.360 --> 00:38:40.940
Can't you do <i>something</i>?

00:38:40.940 --> 00:38:41.840
Bellows!

00:38:43.580 --> 00:38:45.760
Bellows! Hey!

00:38:56.060 --> 00:38:57.210
No response.

00:38:59.700 --> 00:39:05.250
This is Second Lieutenant Ledo,
pilot of Machine Caliber K6821! Anyone?!

00:39:06.360 --> 00:39:07.190
No response.

00:39:07.640 --> 00:39:12.160
It is likely that the Hideauze attack
left them adrift with their reactor exposed.

00:39:12.410 --> 00:39:14.570
Hurry up and restore communications!

00:39:14.570 --> 00:39:15.880
You useless piece of junk!

00:39:15.880 --> 00:39:18.680
It is advised that you refrain from radio transmissions.

00:39:18.680 --> 00:39:19.370
Why?

00:39:19.900 --> 00:39:22.390
Multiple Hideauze life-signs detected.

00:39:22.900 --> 00:39:25.750
They might notice this unit.

00:39:27.080 --> 00:39:28.130
What?

00:39:33.940 --> 00:39:36.560
Are you saying I should just wait to be eaten?

00:39:36.560 --> 00:39:38.060
Activate the emergency beacon!

00:39:38.630 --> 00:39:42.140
I can't leave these decisions up to a machine!

00:39:42.780 --> 00:39:43.860
That is correct.

00:39:45.160 --> 00:39:49.860
As the pilot, you have final call on all decisions,
Second Lieutenant Ledo.

00:39:51.420 --> 00:39:54.600
If you choose to exercise that prerogative
and use your own judgment,

00:39:54.600 --> 00:39:58.680
I will reevaluate the situation
and suggest the best possible course of action.

00:40:00.830 --> 00:40:03.580
So your power depends on me, huh?

00:40:04.030 --> 00:40:05.310
That is correct.

00:40:05.880 --> 00:40:08.920
I await your judgment.

00:40:10.480 --> 00:40:11.370
Very well.

00:40:11.940 --> 00:40:14.530
I'm not going to die here.

00:40:14.530 --> 00:40:17.140
You and I are gonna survive, no matter what!

00:40:17.650 --> 00:40:18.600
Agreed.

00:40:19.530 --> 00:40:24.350
I am an interface system that supports
and oversees the development of pilots.

00:40:24.350 --> 00:40:29.290
I exist solely to set you up for success.

00:40:31.560 --> 00:40:34.160
<i>That's right. Survive.</i>

00:40:34.910 --> 00:40:39.330
<i>He told me I should trust myself.</i>

00:40:39.330 --> 00:40:42.810
<i>And he told me he would trust me.</i>

00:40:46.410 --> 00:40:48.250
<i>I don't have much time.</i>

00:40:48.990 --> 00:40:49.970
<i>Think.</i>

00:40:50.730 --> 00:40:51.720
<i>Think!</i>

00:41:44.850 --> 00:41:46.130
Hurry up!

00:41:46.130 --> 00:41:48.440
Everyone who can dive, get in there!

00:41:48.790 --> 00:41:52.400
Not enough air cylinders!
Scrape together all we've got!

00:41:55.400 --> 00:41:56.820
That's the way!

00:42:01.690 --> 00:42:03.480
Gather the ship captains.

00:42:03.480 --> 00:42:06.180
I'll ask them to supply us
with manpower and resources.

00:42:06.180 --> 00:42:08.590
Get the medics on standby too.

00:42:08.590 --> 00:42:09.400
Roger!

00:42:11.170 --> 00:42:12.750
Amy!

00:42:18.640 --> 00:42:20.470
I'll go save him!

00:42:20.830 --> 00:42:21.580
Leema?

00:42:22.570 --> 00:42:23.940
You can count on me!

00:42:30.340 --> 00:42:31.310
Let's go.

00:42:38.280 --> 00:42:39.560
I'm coming too!

00:42:40.120 --> 00:42:41.280
Amy?

00:42:41.650 --> 00:42:43.050
I want to help!

00:42:44.280 --> 00:42:45.580
Don't be stupid.

00:42:45.580 --> 00:42:47.610
You have other things you need to do.

00:42:48.780 --> 00:42:52.960
When these daredevils come back, we need you to greet them with a smile on your face!

00:42:54.350 --> 00:42:56.450
I'll make sure we get out alive. All of us.

00:42:58.040 --> 00:42:58.960
Okay.

00:43:01.290 --> 00:43:02.480
That's a promise!

00:43:23.680 --> 00:43:24.830
Behind this!

00:43:41.040 --> 00:43:43.150
They still haven't found him?

00:43:49.180 --> 00:43:50.270
Rackage?

00:43:50.670 --> 00:43:53.650
What are you useless fools even doing?

00:43:53.650 --> 00:43:54.440
Make way!

00:43:54.440 --> 00:43:56.530
Here I go!

00:44:03.440 --> 00:44:09.620
Sorry to say, but no one is
allowed to die on my watch!

00:44:09.960 --> 00:44:10.960
Rackage?

00:44:13.960 --> 00:44:15.700
Where is he?

00:44:15.700 --> 00:44:17.130
On the other side of this gap!

00:44:19.330 --> 00:44:20.530
Amico!

00:44:20.530 --> 00:44:22.090
Stronzo!

00:44:33.980 --> 00:44:35.540
Wow...

00:44:35.540 --> 00:44:37.650
Keep it up, Rackage!

00:44:44.380 --> 00:44:45.320
There he is!

00:44:54.340 --> 00:44:55.290
He's alive!

00:44:56.840 --> 00:44:57.750
What?

00:44:59.250 --> 00:45:03.330
"I rerouted the compressed air
from the floaters into the cabin."

00:45:05.310 --> 00:45:07.370
You're quite something, aren't you?

00:45:08.310 --> 00:45:09.180
Listen up, Ledo.

00:45:10.330 --> 00:45:13.210
We'll force the gap open together.

00:45:13.210 --> 00:45:15.850
The moment we do,
detach the limbs and the floaters.

00:45:16.890 --> 00:45:18.690
We only get one chance at this.

00:45:18.690 --> 00:45:20.110
Trust your friends.

00:45:22.470 --> 00:45:23.860
Of course.

00:45:32.390 --> 00:45:34.000
We'll count down from three!

00:45:34.460 --> 00:45:35.210
Three!

00:45:35.650 --> 00:45:36.370
Two!

00:45:36.860 --> 00:45:37.630
One!

00:45:38.070 --> 00:45:39.340
Pull!

00:45:48.800 --> 00:45:50.220
Now, Ledo!

00:45:50.220 --> 00:45:51.470
Got it!

00:46:09.970 --> 00:46:11.580
The machine's free!

00:46:13.070 --> 00:46:14.650
Ledo's all right!

00:46:15.550 --> 00:46:16.580
Hell yeah!

00:46:22.160 --> 00:46:23.440
Amy!

00:46:23.440 --> 00:46:26.250
Thank goodness he's all right!

00:46:56.810 --> 00:46:57.560
Ledo...

00:46:59.680 --> 00:47:00.290
I'm so glad...

00:47:01.280 --> 00:47:03.980
I'm so glad you're safe!

00:47:13.600 --> 00:47:14.490
Amy...

00:47:15.090 --> 00:47:16.260
Glad to be back.

00:49:18.970 --> 00:49:22.100
All right. Proceed to the next phase.

00:49:41.200 --> 00:49:47.950
kore made wa betsu no michi ayundekita futari

00:49:41.200 --> 00:49:47.950
We used to walk different paths

00:49:47.950 --> 00:49:53.960
onaji jikan wo kizamihajimeta n da

00:49:47.950 --> 00:49:53.960
Now our time together has begun

00:49:53.960 --> 00:50:00.590
taisetsu na takaramono katachi wa mienai kedo

00:49:53.960 --> 00:50:00.590
The truly important things are invisible to the eye

00:50:00.590 --> 00:50:06.950
te wo tsunaidara fureta ki ga shita

00:50:00.590 --> 00:50:06.950
I think I know what matters when I touch your hand

00:50:06.950 --> 00:50:13.120
kimi no hitomi ni utsuru atarashii keshiki

00:50:06.950 --> 00:50:13.120
I want to know what the future will be like

00:50:13.120 --> 00:50:21.590
dare yori chikaku de watashi mo issho ni mitsumetai

00:50:13.120 --> 00:50:21.590
I want to hear it directly from you

00:50:21.590 --> 00:50:27.860
oboeteite ne itsumo soba ni iru yo

00:50:21.590 --> 00:50:27.860
Remember, I'm right here

00:50:27.860 --> 00:50:34.170
kore kara mo kimi ga kaeru basho de itai kara

00:50:27.860 --> 00:50:34.170
I want to be there when you return

00:50:34.170 --> 00:50:41.470
